<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leonardo III Tocco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1503</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leonardo III Tocco was the last Tocco ruler of the County Palatine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kefalonia">Cephalonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakynthos">Zakynthos</a> and titular despot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, from 1448. He lost his remaining mainland territories to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, and in 1479 Ottoman forces took Cephalonia, Zakynthos and Lefkada, forcing him to flee to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. He spent his last years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> later took the islands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leonardo-iii-tocco.jpg" alt="Leonardo III Tocco" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlo Sellitto · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leonardo-di-tocco-duke-of-zakynthos-carlo-sellitto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
